                <pb facs="1043" n="1035" sameAs="frus:frus1938v02/pg1035"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">890D.00/697: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Beirut</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Palmer</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Beirut</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1938-06-04T16:00:00+02:00">June 4, 1938—4
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received June 5—11 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Department’s June 3, 7 p.m. Farrell left yesterday with <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >laissez passer</hi> obtained through the High Commission. I have notified
                    Embassy at Ankara that his address is as follows: Princeton Expedition, Antioch.
                    He reports situation calm today and that Commandant Collet, as officer
                    responsible for public security, promises to notify Americans if emergency makes
                    their departure advisable.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Palmer</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
